# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/pushers.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event pr_rival_seat
# en: Somebody's in Your Seat
title [7b2912] = 有人占了你的座位
# en: {~Your table in the library, the good one by the window, is covered in {npc}'s books.|You come back from the shelves and {npc} has moved into your chair, and moved your books to the floor.} {They} look{s} up at you and turn{s} a page, slowly.
text [70cd5a] = {~你在图书馆的那张桌子，靠窗的好位置，堆满了{npc}的书。|你从书架那边回来，{npc}已经坐进了你的椅子，还把你的书挪到了地上。} {They}抬头看了你一眼，慢慢翻过一页。
# en: A library table by a tall window, one student's books spread across all of it, another student standing over it with an armful of their own.
scene [4d39b4] = 高窗边的一张图书馆书桌，一个学生的书摊满了整张桌子，另一个学生抱着一摞自己的书站在旁边。
# en: Sit down opposite and work
opt.left.label [39123c] = 在对面坐下，开始用功
# en: {~You put your books on the one free corner and work as if {they} weren't there. After an hour {npc} pushes a dictionary across without a word. It's almost a truce.|You sit and you work, and you don't look up. {npc} gives up first, packs up with a great deal of noise and leaves you the table.}
opt.left.say.1 [bbd627] = {~你把书放在唯一空着的桌角，当{they}不存在一样埋头用功。一个钟头后，{npc}一言不发地把一本词典推了过来。差不多算休战了。|你坐下就用功，头也不抬。{npc}先撑不住了，大张旗鼓地收拾东西，把桌子让给了你。}
# en: {~{npc} sighs every time you turn a page, then reads your notes upside down and corrects them aloud. You last twenty minutes.|{They} hum{s}. {They} tap{s}. {They} sharpen{s} a quill for a quarter of an hour. You leave, and hear {them} spread out again behind you.}
opt.left.say.2 [ed4f4c] = {~你每翻一页{npc}就叹一口气，然后倒着读你的笔记，还大声纠错。你只撑了二十分钟。|{They}哼歌。{They}敲桌子。{They}削一支羽毛笔削了一刻钟。你走了，听见身后{them}又把东西摊开了。}
# en: Find another table
opt.right.label [970a5d] = 另找一张桌子
# en: {~You take a table by the draughty door, which is worse, and get your reading done anyway. {npc} watches you go with the look of someone keeping score.|There's a desk in the stacks with no window and no {npc}. You work well there, and hate that {they} chose it for you.}
opt.right.say.1 [7b9241] = {~你挑了张靠漏风的门的桌子，更糟，但书照样读完了。{npc}看着你走开，一副在记分的样子。|书库里有张没窗户、也没有{npc}的书桌。你在那儿效率很高，却恨这是{they}替你挑的。}

@event pr_rival_book
# en: The Only Copy
title [57f157] = 唯一的一本
# en: {~The essay is due on Friday, and the library has one copy of the book it needs.|There's one copy of this week's set book in the whole library.} {npc} has it. {They} {are} reading it at lunch, at the end of your table, one page at a time, with a finger under every line. "Nearly done," {they} say{s}, without looking up. "Another week, perhaps."
text [181fba] = {~论文星期五交，图书馆里需要的那本书只有一本。|这星期的指定读物，整个图书馆只有一本。}在{npc}手里。{They}在午饭时读它，就坐在你这张桌子的另一头，一次一页，手指压着每一行。“快读完了，”{they}头也不抬地说，“大概再要一个星期吧。”
# en: A busy refectory at lunch, a student reading a thick library book very slowly at the end of a table, another student watching from across the room.
scene [388d9a] = 午饭时热闹的膳堂，一个学生在长桌一头极慢地读一本厚厚的图书馆藏书，另一个学生从房间那头看着。
# en: Ask to share it
opt.left.label [87e601] = 请求一起看
# en: {~You ask, properly, and don't make a joke of it. {npc} looks at you for a long moment, then turns the book sideways so you can both read. You finish the chapter together without a word, and {they} hand{s} it over on Thursday.|"Fine," says {npc}, as if it costs {them} something. It does: {they} let{s} you copy the chapter, and at the end {they} say{s}, "Your essay had better be worse than mine."}
opt.left.say.1 [b50c0b] = {~你正正经经地开口，没拿它开玩笑。{npc}看了你好一会儿，然后把书侧过来，让你们俩都能看。你们一言不发地读完了那一章，星期四{they}把书交给了你。|“行吧，”{npc}说，好像这让{them}付出了什么。确实如此：{they}让你抄了那一章，最后说：“你的论文最好比我的差。”}
# en: {~"No," says {npc}, pleasantly, and turns a page. You write the essay from your lecture notes and a bad memory, and it shows.|{npc} pretends not to hear you, then reads a paragraph aloud to the table, very slowly. It's the paragraph you needed. You still don't have the book.}
opt.left.say.2 [3d55ef] = {~“不行，”{npc}客客气气地说，又翻了一页。你只能靠课堂笔记和糟糕的记性写论文，看得出来。|{npc}假装没听见，然后慢悠悠地对着全桌念了一段。正是你需要的那一段。书还是不在你手里。}
# en: Buy your own copy in the village
opt.right.label [4810e9] = 去村里自己买一本
# en: {~Grimsby has a copy, a little foxed, at a price that makes you wince. You finish the essay a day early. {npc} returns the library's copy that afternoon, unread past chapter two.|You walk down to the village and pay too much for a second-hand copy. On the way back you pass {npc} in the library, returning the book, done with it at last.}
opt.right.say.1 [b61bc8] = {~格林斯比有一本，有点泛黄，价钱让你肉疼。你提前一天写完了论文。{npc}当天下午就把图书馆那本还了，第二章以后一页没读。|你走到村里，花冤枉钱买了本二手的。回来路上，你看见{npc}在图书馆还书，总算读完了。}

@event pr_rival_race
# en: To the Far Jetty
title [5c068a] = 划到远处的码头
# en: {npc} is at the boathouse slip with two boats out and a crowd on the boards. "To the far jetty and back," {they} say{s}, loud enough for all of them. "Loser carries the winner's books for a week." Somebody is already taking bets.
text [a2ca0f] = {npc}在船屋的下水坡道上，放出了两条船，栈板上围了一群人。“划到远处的码头再回来，”{they}说，声音大得让所有人都听得见，“输的人替赢的人背一个星期书。”已经有人开始下注了。
# en: Two rowing boats side by side at a boathouse slip, a student already at the oars in one, a small crowd gathering on the boards.
scene [c7ab76] = 船屋下水坡道上并排停着两条划艇，一个学生已经握着桨坐进其中一条，栈板上聚起一小群人。
# en: Take the other boat
opt.left.label [187423] = 上另一条船
# en: {~You touch the far jetty first and turn so hard you nearly swamp. You come in a length ahead, soaked to the elbow. {npc} carries your books for a week, with enormous dignity.|You win by a boat's nose. The boards cheer. {npc} carries your books for a week and drops them, accidentally, every day.}
opt.left.say.1 [00599e] = {~你先碰到远处的码头，掉头掉得太猛，差点把船灌满水。你领先一个船身回来，袖子湿到胳膊肘。{npc}替你背了一星期的书，背得极有尊严。|你赢了一个船头。栈板上一片欢呼。{npc}替你背了一星期的书，每天都“不小心”掉一次。}
# en: {~{npc} is back at the slip, shipping oars, before you've turned at the far jetty. You carry {their} books for a week. On the fourth day {they} take{s} half of them back without a word.|You catch a crab at the turn and go in backwards. For a week you carry two bags to every class, and {npc} finds the heaviest books {they} can.}
opt.left.say.2 [bdde9e] = {~你还没在远处的码头掉头，{npc}已经回到坡道，收起了桨。你替{them}背了一星期的书。第四天，{they}一言不发地拿回了一半。|你在掉头时一桨划空，船倒着进了水。一个星期里，你每节课都背着两个书包，{npc}还专挑最重的书给你。}
# en: Watch from the boards
opt.right.label [1c160c] = 站在栈板上看
# en: {~You let {them} row against nobody. {npc} comes back flushed and wins nothing, and tells you so. The crowd thinks less of you, and you keep your feet dry.|"Scared," says {npc}, climbing out. "Dry," you say. Half the boards agree with each of you.}
opt.right.say.1 [19b36e] = {~你让{them}跟空气比赛。{npc}满脸通红地回来，什么也没赢到，还专门来告诉你。大家都看低了你，但你的脚是干的。|“胆小鬼，”{npc}边爬上来边说。“干爽，”你说。栈板上的人一半站你这边，一半站{their}那边。}

@event pr_rival_signed_up
# en: Volunteered
title [82cdc8] = 被自愿
# en: There's a list on the classroom door: volunteers to demonstrate a spell in front of the whole year on Friday. Your name is on it, in handwriting that isn't yours. {npc}, passing, says, "Good luck," and means the opposite.
text [3d3f5f] = 教室门上贴了张名单：星期五在全年级面前演示咒语的志愿者。上面有你的名字，笔迹不是你的。{npc}经过时说了声“祝你好运”，意思正相反。
# en: A notice pinned to a classroom door listing volunteers for a demonstration before the whole year, one name in different handwriting.
scene [8e5bbd] = 教室门上钉着一张名单，列着要在全年级面前演示的志愿者，其中一个名字的笔迹与众不同。
# en: Go through with it
opt.left.label [e23b0f] = 硬着头皮上
# en: {~You give the best demonstration of the week. The professor asks you to do it again, slower. {npc}, in the front row, claps three times, exactly.|It goes perfectly. Afterwards {npc} says it was "lucky", which is the closest {they}'ll ever come to saying "well done".}
opt.left.say.1 [2ac561] = {~你做了这周最好的一场演示。教授让你再慢点来一遍。坐在前排的{npc}拍了三下手，不多不少。|一切完美。事后{npc}说那是“运气”，这已经是{they}最接近“干得好”的说法了。}
# en: {~It goes wrong in front of everyone, and keeps going wrong. {npc} doesn't laugh, which is somehow worse. Later {they} say{s}, "I didn't think you'd actually do it."|The spell fizzles. A first-year in the front row says "oh" in a small, sad voice. {npc} looks almost sorry, for nearly a second.}
opt.left.say.2 [2baedb] = {~当着所有人的面出了岔子，而且一错再错。{npc}没笑，不知怎么反倒更糟。后来{they}说：“我没想到你真会上。”|咒语哑了火。前排一个一年级生小小地、难过地“哦”了一声。{npc}看上去几乎有点抱歉，差不多持续了一秒。}
# en: Cross your name off
opt.right.label [76f458] = 把名字划掉
# en: {~You strike the name out and write "NOT ME" next to it, and the whole corridor sees you do it. By Friday the list has three more names on it in {npc}'s handwriting, and they're all {their} friends'.|You cross it off in front of {them}. "Shame," says {npc}. "I was looking forward to it." You were not.}
opt.right.say.1 [9970f3] = {~你划掉名字，在旁边写上“不是我”，整条走廊都看见了。到星期五，名单上又多了三个{npc}笔迹写的名字，全是{their}朋友。|你当着{them}的面划掉了。“可惜了，”{npc}说，“我还挺期待的。”你可不期待。}

@event lyra_rival_seat
# en: The Table by the Window
title [e68d82] = 靠窗的桌子
# en: It's late, and Lyra has your table in the library: the one by the window, the one you've had all term. Her books are on both chairs. "It's a library," she says, without looking up. "Not a pew. Sit somewhere you can win."
text [92a19a] = 夜深了，莱拉占了你在图书馆的桌子：靠窗的那张，你坐了一整个学期的那张。两把椅子上都堆着她的书。“这是图书馆，”她头也不抬地说，“不是教堂长椅。去坐个你赢得了的地方。”
# en: A library at night, a red-haired student alone at a table by the window with a stack of fire-theory books, a second chair pulled out and piled with them too.
scene [f92b77] = 夜里的图书馆，一个红发学生独自坐在靠窗的桌前，面前一摞火焰理论的书，另一把拉开的椅子上也堆满了书。
# en: Clear a chair and sit down
opt.left.label [bced5b] = 清出一把椅子坐下
# en: {~You move her books, carefully, in order, and sit. She stares. Then she goes back to reading, and at midnight, without looking up, she slides you the one book on the table you needed.|You stack her books on the floor by size and open your own. She is speechless for a whole minute, which may be a record. You work until the lamps go out, side by side, not speaking.}
opt.left.say.1 [5838f6] = {~你把她的书小心地、按顺序挪开，坐下。她瞪着你。然后她接着读书，到了午夜，头也不抬地把桌上你正需要的那本书推了过来。|你把她的书按大小摞在地上，打开自己的。她整整一分钟说不出话，大概破了纪录。你们并排坐着用功，一言不发，直到熄灯。}
# en: {~You sit. She reads aloud from your notes, upside down, and corrects your fire-theory in a whisper the whole library can hear. You last until the second correction.|You sit down and she turns up her lamp until it's like reading next to the sun. "If I'm awake," she says, "I see no reason you should be able to think."}
opt.left.say.2 [d0430d] = {~你坐下了。她倒着念你的笔记，用整个图书馆都听得见的耳语纠正你的火焰理论。你撑到第二处纠错就走了。|你一坐下，她就把灯调亮，亮得像在太阳边上看书。“既然我醒着，”她说，“我看不出你有什么理由能好好思考。”}
# en: Leave her the window
opt.right.label [ce2d20] = 把窗边让给她
# en: {~You take the desk in the stacks. It's quiet, and you get your reading done. When you leave at midnight she's still at the window, alone with nine books, not reading any of them.|You go. Behind you she says, "Coward," to the page, and turns it too hard.}
opt.right.say.1 [d0e9da] = {~你去了书库里的书桌。那里很安静，你把书读完了。午夜离开时，她还坐在窗边，独自守着九本书，一本也没在读。|你走了。身后她对着书页说了声“胆小鬼”，翻页翻得太用力。}

@event lyra_rival_signed_up
# en: Second on the List
title [9c0d3f] = 名单上的第二个
# en: The list for Friday's demonstration before the whole year is up on the classroom door. At the top, in tight upright capitals: VANESHADE. Directly beneath it, in the same hand, is your name. Lyra, passing, doesn't stop. "Everyone should see the difference," she says.
text [039917] = 星期五在全年级面前演示的名单贴在了教室门上。最上面，用紧凑挺直的大写字母写着：凡妮希德。紧挨着下面，同样的笔迹，是你的名字。莱拉经过时没停步。“大家应该看看差别，”她说。
# en: A list of volunteers pinned to a classroom door, a name in tight upright capitals at the top and another name squeezed in directly beneath it.
scene [0e61c3] = 教室门上钉着一张志愿者名单，最上面是一个紧凑挺直的大写名字，另一个名字紧挨着挤在下面。
# en: Go on straight after her
opt.left.label [8a8303] = 紧接着她上场
# en: {~She's brilliant, and the hall applauds, and then you're better. Not by much. Enough. On the way out she says, without turning round, "Again. Next term." It's the nearest she has to a compliment.|You match her flame for flame. The professor, confused, gives you both full marks. Lyra looks at the marks as if they'd insulted her family.}
opt.left.say.1 [cd32d7] = {~她很出色，全场鼓掌，然后你更好。没好太多。但够了。出门时她头也不回地说：“再来。下学期。”这是她最接近夸奖的话。|你和她一招一招地打成平手。教授一头雾水，给了你们俩满分。莱拉看着那分数，好像它侮辱了她的家族。}
# en: {~After hers, yours looks like a candle at noon. Lyra doesn't smile. She seems, if anything, disappointed. "I thought you'd do better," she says, and it sounds like the truth.|It fizzles. Lyra, in the front row, is very still. Afterwards she stops beside you. "Wrist," she says. "You lead with the wrist." Then she's gone.}
opt.left.say.2 [df81cf] = {~在她之后，你的像正午的一根蜡烛。莱拉没笑。她看上去甚至有些失望。“我以为你会做得更好，”她说，听起来是真心话。|哑火了。坐在前排的莱拉一动不动。事后她在你身边停下。“手腕，”她说，“你用手腕起手。”然后就走了。}
# en: Cross your name off
opt.right.label [76f458] = 把名字划掉
# en: {~You strike yourself off. On Friday she demonstrates alone, perfectly, to polite applause, and looks once at the empty place on the list.|You cross it out. "Afraid of the comparison," she says. "Bored of it," you say. Neither of you believes the other.}
opt.right.say.1 [0c45fa] = {~你把自己划掉了。星期五她独自演示，完美无缺，赢得礼貌的掌声，然后看了一眼名单上的空位。|你划掉了。“怕被比较，”她说。“比腻了，”你说。谁都不信对方。}

@event bram_rival_race
# en: Prefect's Privilege
title [996b59] = 级长特权
# en: Bram is in the courtyard before breakfast with his sash on and his ledger out. "Three laps of the cloister," he says. "Lose, and it's a demerit for loitering. Win, and..." He thinks. "And nothing. Prefect's privilege." The first-years in the cloister are delighted.
text [9e28e6] = 早饭前，布拉姆就戴着绶带、拿着记过簿站在庭院里。“绕回廊跑三圈，”他说，“输了，记一次‘闲逛’。赢了，就……”他想了想，“就什么也没有。级长特权。”回廊里的一年级生乐坏了。
# en: A courtyard at dawn, a broad prefect in a red sash at the start of a chalk line, a student beside him, first-years watching from the cloister.
scene [edfb67] = 黎明的庭院，一个佩红色绶带的魁梧级长站在粉笔起跑线前，一个学生站在他旁边，一年级生们在回廊里看着。
# en: Run the laps
opt.left.label [1f8bd1] = 跑
# en: {~You beat him by a step on the last turn. He's purple, and furious, and then, unexpectedly, he laughs. "Fine," he says. "No demerit." He writes something in the ledger anyway. Later you see it's your time.|You win. Bram stands with his hands on his knees and gives the first-years a demerit each for cheering. Not you, though.}
opt.left.say.1 [4a0e42] = {~你在最后一个弯道领先他一步。他脸涨得发紫，气坏了，然后出乎意料地笑了。“行，”他说，“不记过。”他还是在记过簿上写了点什么。后来你才看到，那是你的成绩。|你赢了。布拉姆双手撑着膝盖，给每个欢呼的一年级生记了一次过。没记你。}
# en: {~He's a lap ahead by the end, sash flying. "Loitering," he says, and writes it down, with the time. The first-years are less delighted now.|You lose, and get the demerit, and he reads it out to the cloister: "For loitering. At a run."}
opt.left.say.2 [5b8be5] = {~最后他领先你一圈，绶带飘着。“闲逛，”他说，记下来，连时间一起。一年级生们没那么乐了。|你输了，被记了过，他还当着整个回廊念出来：“闲逛。跑着闲逛。”}
# en: "That's not a rule, Bram"
opt.right.label [c11c2a] = “没这条规矩，布拉姆”
# en: {~"It is now," he says. You quote him the actual rule on loitering, word for word, from the student handbook, and he goes red and lets you past. He'll remember it.|"Show me where it's written." He can't. He tells you he'll find it. Every morning for a week he's in the courtyard, reading the handbook.}
opt.right.say.1 [dae9bf] = {~“现在有了，”他说。你把学生手册里关于闲逛的真正规定一字不差地背给他听，他脸一红，放你过去了。他会记住这事的。|“写在哪儿了？给我看看。”他拿不出来。他说他会找到的。整整一星期，每天早上他都在庭院里翻学生手册。}

@event bram_rival_signed_up
# en: The Duty Rota
title [08176c] = 值日表
# en: The prefects' duty rota is up outside the common room. Someone has put your name down for every Saturday morning this month, scrubbing the east staircase, in heavy capitals. Bram is standing beside it with his arms folded. "Volunteered," he says. "Very public-spirited."
text [3a2681] = 级长值日表贴在了公共休息室外面。有人用粗重的大写字母，把你的名字填进了这个月每个星期六上午的空格：擦洗东楼梯。布拉姆抱着胳膊站在旁边。“自愿的，”他说，“很有公益精神。”
# en: A prefects' rota pinned outside a common room, a student's name written in every Saturday slot in heavy capitals.
scene [ba544b] = 公共休息室外钉着一张级长值日表，每个星期六的格子里都用粗重的大写字母写着同一个学生的名字。
# en: Scrub it, every Saturday
opt.left.label [5309a7] = 每个星期六都去擦
# en: {~Four Saturdays on your knees on the east staircase. On the last one, Bram turns up with a second brush and does the top flight himself, without a word. "Missed a bit," he says.|You scrub it so well that it shines. By the third Saturday people are using another staircase so as not to spoil it, and Bram, passing, says, "Huh."}
opt.left.say.1 [ee6a25] = {~四个星期六，你跪在东楼梯上擦。最后一个星期六，布拉姆拿着第二把刷子来了，一言不发地把最上面一段擦了。“漏了一块，”他说。|你擦得锃亮。到第三个星期六，大家都绕道走别的楼梯，免得踩脏了，布拉姆经过时说了声：“哈。”}
# en: Take it to the head prefect
opt.right.label [f8f7fc] = 去找学生会长
# en: {~The head prefect looks at the handwriting, then at Bram, and moves your name to his. Bram scrubs the east staircase every Saturday this month. He looks at you every Saturday too.|Struck off. Bram is put on the rota himself, "for public spirit". He doesn't speak to you, or to the head prefect, for a fortnight.}
opt.right.say.1 [714a9f] = {~学生会长看看笔迹，又看看布拉姆，把你的名字改成了他的。这个月每个星期六，布拉姆都在擦东楼梯。每个星期六他也都盯着你看。|名字被划掉了。布拉姆自己被排上了值日表，“以表彰其公益精神”。两个星期里他既不跟你说话，也不跟学生会长说话。}
# en: {~"He's a prefect," says the head prefect. "If he says you volunteered, you volunteered." You scrub the staircase. Bram inspects it every Saturday, with a white glove.|Your complaint goes on file next to the rota. You do the Saturdays anyway, and Bram adds one, for "complaining".}
opt.right.say.2 [1b9cf0] = {~“他是级长，”学生会长说，“他说你是自愿的，你就是自愿的。”你去擦了楼梯。每个星期六布拉姆都戴着白手套来检查。|你的投诉被归档在值日表旁边。你照样去擦了那几个星期六，布拉姆又给你加了一个，理由是“投诉”。}

@event grisk_kind_month
# en: A Kind Month
title [911a54] = 宽厚的一个月
# en: Grisk waves you over at the Newt and slides this month's envelope back across the table to you, unopened. "You have been very regular," he purrs. "I like regular. So this month, as a friend, I'll take nothing at all." He holds up one square of ledger paper. "In return, you'll owe me one small kindness. When I ask. A friendship goes both ways."
text [63f490] = 格里斯克在镀金蝾螈酒馆招手叫你过去，把这个月的信封原封不动地推回到你面前。“你一直很准时，”他轻声细语地说，“我喜欢准时。所以这个月，作为朋友，我分文不取。”他举起一小方账页纸。“作为回报，你欠我一个小小的人情。等我开口时还。友谊是双向的嘛。”
# en: A goblin in a velvet waistcoat at a tavern table, tearing one small square out of a ledger page with great care.
scene [831c42] = 酒馆的一张桌旁，一个穿天鹅绒背心的地精小心翼翼地从账页上撕下一小方纸。
# en: Take the month off
opt.left.label [c9a1fa] = 这个月就免了吧
# en: He tears the square out and folds it into his waistcoat pocket, next to his heart, if goblins keep them there. The envelope goes back in your purse. You can feel the folded paper all the way back up the hill.
opt.left.say.1 [479d6c] = 他撕下那方纸，折好放进背心口袋，贴着心口——如果地精有心的话。信封回到了你的钱袋里。一路走回山上，你都感觉得到那张折起来的纸。
# en: Pay as usual
opt.right.label [f47e19] = 照常付
# en: "As you like," says Grisk, and takes the envelope back, and puts the square away, unfolded. "Kindness keeps." You leave lighter in the purse and somehow lighter everywhere else.
opt.right.say.1 [826d56] = “随你，”格里斯克说，收回信封，把那方纸原样收了起来，没折。“人情放着不会坏。”你离开时钱袋轻了，别处却莫名轻松了。

@event grisk_settle_early
# en: Settling Up
title [c3cc72] = 了结
# en: Grisk sits down across from you at Mabel's without asking and orders for you both. "I hear you've been fortunate," he says, with a glance at your purse. "So, a courtesy. Pay me most of what's left, today, and I'll close your page. You'll save a little. I'll save the bother of you."
text [8f6579] = 格里斯克没问一声就在梅布尔茶馆你对面坐下，替你们俩点了茶。“听说你最近手头宽裕，”他瞥了一眼你的钱袋，“那么，给你个方便。今天把剩下的大头付了，我就合上你这一页。你省一点。我省得麻烦你。”
# en: A goblin moneylender's ledger open on a café table, a column of figures, a pen offered with a little bow.
scene [1766c8] = 茶馆桌上摊开着一个地精放贷人的账本，一列数字，一支笔被微微欠身递了过来。
# en: Pay him off and close the page
opt.left.label [087b93] = 付清，合上这一页
# en: He counts the coins twice, then draws a neat line under your name and blots it. "A pleasure," he says, "and a loss." You walk out owing nobody anything, and the tea is on your bill.
opt.left.say.1 [7d71c6] = 他把钱数了两遍，然后在你名字下面整整齐齐画了一道线，吸干墨迹。“荣幸之至，”他说，“也是损失。”你走出门时谁也不欠了，茶钱记在你账上。
# en: Keep to the monthly plan
opt.right.label [7aba96] = 还是按月来
# en: "Of course," says Grisk. "Twelve a month is a lovely rhythm." He pays for the tea, which feels like an investment, and it is one.
opt.right.say.1 [70602e] = “当然，”格里斯克说，“一个月十二，节奏多好。”他付了茶钱，像是一笔投资，也确实是。

@event grisk_interest_in_kind
# en: Interest in Kind
title [deced0] = 以物抵息
# en: "I don't need your crowns this month," Grisk says, in the square, falling into step. "I need to know things. Who in your year is short. Who has been to the pawnbroker. Who has a parent who'd pay to keep a little trouble quiet." He smiles. "One name, and a month comes off."
text [048b0e] = “这个月我不要你的克朗，”格里斯克在广场上走到你身边说，“我要知道些事情。你们年级谁手头紧。谁去过当铺。谁的父母愿意花钱把一点小麻烦压下去。”他笑了笑，“一个名字，抵一个月。”
# en: A goblin in pince-nez walking beside a student across a village square, a quill poised above an open ledger, the student looking away.
scene [b2ea1d] = 一个戴夹鼻眼镜的地精走在穿过村庄广场的学生身旁，羽毛笔悬在摊开的账本上方，学生把目光移开了。
# en: Give him a name
opt.left.label [85d078] = 给他一个名字
# en: You give him a name, someone who's been asking around for a loan anyway. Grisk writes it down without a word and crosses a month off the end of your page. A week later you see them with Grisk at the Newt, laughing at something he's said.
opt.left.say.1 [ceaf83] = 你给了他一个名字，一个本来就在到处找人借钱的人。格里斯克一言不发地记下，在你那页末尾划掉了一个月。一星期后，你看见那人和格里斯克在镀金蝾螈酒馆里，被他说的什么话逗得直笑。
# en: "I don't know anybody's business"
opt.right.label [518d61] = “我不打听别人的事”
# en: "Admirable," says Grisk, "and rare," and leaves your page exactly as long as it was. "Do let me know if you ever start."
opt.right.say.1 [a9a98b] = “令人钦佩，”格里斯克说，“也很少见。”你那一页一行也没少。“哪天你开始打听了，记得告诉我。”

@event grisk_troll_letter
# en: A Letter Home, for a Troll
title [6b18d2] = 替巨魔写家书
# en: A troll in a very tight waistcoat is sitting outside the Newt with a pencil in his fist and a letter he can't finish. "I collect for Mister Grisk," he rumbles, by way of introduction. "Politely. He says you're a scholar. It's to my mother. I want it to sound like I'm doing well."
text [6be36b] = 一个穿着紧绷背心的巨魔坐在镀金蝾螈酒馆外面，拳头里捏着一支铅笔，面前是一封写不下去的信。“我替格里斯克先生收账，”他闷声说，算是自我介绍，“很客气地收。他说你是个读书人。这是写给我母亲的。我想让她觉得我过得很好。”
# en: A very large troll in a tight waistcoat on a bench outside a tavern, holding a crumpled letter and a pencil in an enormous fist.
scene [3223b0] = 酒馆外的长凳上坐着一个穿紧绷背心的大块头巨魔，巨大的拳头里攥着一封皱巴巴的信和一支铅笔。
# en: Help him write it
opt.left.label [5473a4] = 帮他写
# en: An hour on the bench, with your own reading left in your bag, and a letter in your best hand about a son in steady work in a respectable trade, in the village, with prospects. All true, if you squint. He reads it back with his lips moving and shakes your hand very gently, as if it might come off.
opt.left.say.1 [11cd86] = 在长凳上坐了一个钟头，自己的书还躺在包里，你用最好看的字写了一封信：一个儿子在村里干着一份体面的稳定营生，前途不错。眯着眼看的话，句句属实。他动着嘴唇把信念了一遍，然后非常轻地跟你握了握手，好像怕把你的手握掉。
# en: Say you've an essay to finish
opt.right.label [454cf3] = 说你还有论文要写
# en: He nods slowly and goes back to the pencil. When you come past again at closing time, he's still there, on the first line.
opt.right.say.1 [3cf336] = 他慢慢点点头，又低头对付那支铅笔。到了打烊时分你再经过，他还在那儿，停在第一行。

@event grisk_regards_friend
# en: Do Give My Regards
title [074b41] = 代我问好
# en: Grisk takes this month's payment with a bow. "And do give my regards to {friend}," he adds. "Such a good friend to you. It would be a pity if {they} heard about our little friendship from anyone but you." He says it like a remark about the weather.
text [d60c62] = 格里斯克收下这个月的钱，欠了欠身。“还有，代我向{friend}问好，”他补充道，“对你多好的朋友啊。要是{they}从别人嘴里听说了我们这点小交情，那多可惜。”他说得就像在谈天气。
# en: A goblin in a velvet waistcoat taking his receipt with a little bow, saying something pleasant, a student's smile frozen.
scene [115ea0] = 一个穿天鹅绒背心的地精微微欠身收下收据，说着客气话，一个学生的笑容僵在脸上。
# en: Tell {friend} yourself
opt.left.label [3c2c7b] = 自己告诉{friend}
# en: You tell {friend} that evening, all of it. {They} {are} quiet, then angry, though not at you. "He said that? Pay him off and never go near him again." Grisk, next month, seems a little less pleased with himself.
opt.left.say.1 [979af9] = 当晚你就把一切都告诉了{friend}。{They}先是沉默，然后生气了，但不是冲你。“他这么说？赶紧还清，再也别靠近他。”下个月，格里斯克似乎没那么得意了。
# en: Pay him a little extra to forget
opt.right.label [d03594] = 多付他一点，让他忘了
# en: You add a few crowns to the envelope. Grisk weighs it in his palm and nods. "Forgotten," he says. "I have a terrible memory." He doesn't. He has a ledger.
opt.right.say.1 [eaeecd] = 你往信封里多塞了几个克朗。格里斯克在手心掂了掂，点点头。“忘了，”他说，“我记性坏得很。”他没有。他有账本。

@event ember_and_footnote
# en: The Fox and the Cat
title [e88a17] = 狐狸与猫
# en: Ember has followed you into the library, which she has never done, and found Footnote, the library cat, on his table. They are nose to nose. Nobody in the room is breathing. Ember's tail has begun, very gently, to smoke. The librarian is coming down the aisle at speed.
text [6e0fa3] = 余烬跟着你进了图书馆，这是从没有过的事，还在桌上找到了图书馆的猫脚注。它们鼻子对着鼻子。屋里谁都不敢喘气。余烬的尾巴开始非常轻地冒烟。图书管理员正快步沿着过道走过来。
# en: A library aisle, a small fire-tailed fox and a large grey cat nose to nose on a reading table, every student in the room frozen mid-page, a librarian on the move.
scene [d8ff94] = 图书馆过道里，一只尾巴带火的小狐狸和一只大灰猫在阅览桌上鼻子对鼻子，屋里每个学生都僵在翻页的动作上，一位图书管理员正疾步赶来。
# en: Scoop her up and leave
opt.left.label [166fdf] = 一把抱起她就走
# en: You get her under your arm before anything happens and walk out with your books abandoned on the table. Ember sulks all the way back to the tower. Footnote, the librarian tells you later, sat on your notes until closing, out of victory.
opt.left.say.1 [fb9260] = 在出事之前你把她夹到胳膊底下，书都扔在桌上就走了。余烬一路生着闷气回到塔里。图书管理员后来告诉你，脚注在你的笔记上一直坐到闭馆，以示胜利。
# en: Let them settle it
opt.right.label [c04cd0] = 让它们自己解决
# en: Footnote yawns, turns round twice and lies down. Ember considers this, then lies down beside him with her chin on his back. The whole library breathes out. The librarian stops, looks, and says, "Well, don't wake them."
opt.right.say.1 [4e2ddf] = 脚注打了个哈欠，转了两圈，躺下了。余烬想了想，也在它身边躺下，下巴搁在它背上。整个图书馆都松了口气。图书管理员停下来看了看，说：“那就别吵醒它们。”
# en: Footnote swats once and Ember's tail flares. A shelf of periodicals is singed before you can get her out, and the librarian sends you the bill for the bindings. Footnote is entirely unhurt and very pleased with himself.
opt.right.say.2 [d45e3e] = 脚注挥了一爪，余烬的尾巴腾地燃起来。你还没把她弄出去，一架期刊就被燎焦了，图书管理员把装订费的账单寄给了你。脚注毫发无伤，得意得很。

@event ember_ring
# en: The Ring in the Ashes
title [e40a8e] = 灰烬里的戒指
# en: There's a ring in your cold hearth this morning, a small tarnished gold one, engraved inside with two sets of initials, and Ember is sitting beside it, looking modest. She has brought it from somewhere. She will not say where.
text [c8d049] = 今天早上，你冰冷的壁炉里躺着一枚戒指，一枚失了光泽的小金戒，内圈刻着两组姓名缩写。余烬坐在旁边，一副谦虚的样子。她是从哪儿弄来的。她不肯说。
# en: A dormitory hearth in the morning, a small fox sitting proudly beside a tarnished gold ring in the cold ashes.
scene [9fe28e] = 清晨宿舍的壁炉，一只小狐狸骄傲地坐在冷灰里一枚失了光泽的金戒指旁。
# en: Ask around the village for its owner
opt.left.label [7334f6] = 去村里打听失主
# en: It takes two afternoons. In the end it belongs to the baker's mother, who lost it in her garden forty years ago and had stopped looking. She cries, and gives you a loaf every Saturday for a month, and a second, smaller one "for the fox".
opt.left.say.1 [99cad6] = 花了两个下午。最后发现它属于面包师的母亲，四十年前丢在了自家花园里，早就不找了。她哭了，接下来一个月每个星期六都送你一个面包，外加一个小一点的，“给狐狸的”。
# en: Sell it at the pawnbroker's
opt.right.label [48fbcd] = 拿去当铺卖了
# en: The pawnbroker gives you a fair price and doesn't ask. Ember watches you hand it over, and something in the set of her ears says she'd meant it for you to keep.
opt.right.say.1 [5a4bfa] = 当铺老板给了个公道价，什么也没问。余烬看着你把它递过去，她耳朵的姿势分明在说：她本来是想让你留着的。

@event ember_out_till_dawn
# en: Not Back by Dawn
title [61a4d8] = 天亮了还没回来
# en: Ember went out of the window at midnight, as she does. She isn't back. It's dawn, the saucer is full, and there's a faint line of smoke above the trees at the forest's edge.
text [8f4a01] = 余烬半夜从窗户出去了，她一向如此。她还没回来。天已经亮了，碟子里的奶还满着，森林边缘的树梢上方有一缕淡淡的烟。
# en: An empty windowsill at dawn, a saucer of milk untouched, a student in a coat looking out towards a forest's edge.
scene [879cd4] = 黎明时空荡荡的窗台，一碟没动过的牛奶，一个穿外套的学生望向森林边缘。
# en: Go out to the forest's edge
opt.left.label [3f584b] = 去森林边上找她
# en: You find her in the bracken beside the smoke, which is only her, curled up and asleep with three wild foxes of her own colour, all of them smouldering gently. She wakes, looks at you and yawns, then walks home at your heels as if it had been your idea.
opt.left.say.1 [3b27ec] = 你在烟旁边的蕨丛里找到了她——那烟就是她自己——她蜷着睡着了，身边是三只和她一样毛色的野狐狸，全都轻轻地冒着烟。她醒来，看看你，打了个哈欠，然后跟在你脚边走回家，好像这是你的主意。
# en: Wait, and go back to bed
opt.right.label [353c0a] = 等着，回去睡觉
# en: You go back to bed and doze, badly, until the bell, then go to your lecture and hear none of it. When you get back she's on your pillow, smelling of woodsmoke and very pleased with herself, and she won't explain.
opt.right.say.1 [988542] = 你回到床上，迷迷糊糊地打着盹，一直到钟响，然后去上课，什么也没听进去。回来时她已经在你枕头上了，一身木烟味，得意得很，什么也不肯解释。

@event ember_mouse
# en: Somebody's Mouse
title [948e50] = 谁家的老鼠
# en: Ember has brought you a mouse. It's alive, white, very clean and wearing a tiny green ribbon. On your way to breakfast you pass a notice on the corridor wall: LOST, ONE MOUSE (FAMILIAR), WHITE, GREEN RIBBON, FIRST-YEAR DORMITORY, PLEASE.
text [de963e] = 余烬给你带来了一只老鼠。活的，白的，非常干净，还系着一根小小的绿缎带。去吃早饭的路上，你看见走廊墙上贴着一张告示：寻：老鼠一只（魔宠），白色，系绿缎带，请送一年级宿舍，拜托了。
# en: A small fire-tailed fox sitting on a dormitory floor with a very much alive white mouse held gently between her paws, a lost-familiar notice pinned to the door beyond.
scene [7adb7c] = 宿舍地板上，一只尾巴带火的小狐狸用两只前爪轻轻按着一只活生生的白老鼠，门外钉着一张寻找魔宠的告示。
# en: Take the mouse back
opt.left.label [8fd5b1] = 把老鼠送回去
# en: The first-year bursts into tears and hugs you, then the mouse, then you again. Ember, who had plans, sulks under the bed until supper and won't touch her milk.
opt.left.say.1 [8c13ac] = 那个一年级生哭着抱住你，又抱老鼠，又抱你。本来另有打算的余烬在床底下生闷气到晚饭，连奶都不碰。
# en: Let Ember have her fun a day
opt.right.label [e9a63a] = 让余烬玩上一天
# en: Ember and the mouse spend the day in the warm by your hearth, the fox watching it as if it were the finest thing ever made. You return it that night, quietly, through the door, and say nothing. The first-year spends a day in tears first.
opt.right.say.1 [02a4c5] = 余烬和老鼠在你的壁炉边暖洋洋地待了一天，狐狸盯着它，好像那是世上最精致的东西。那天晚上你悄悄从门缝里把它送了回去，什么也没说。那个一年级生先哭了一整天。

@event ember_old_coin
# en: From the Walls
title [582567] = 从墙里来的
# en: Ember squeezes out from behind a corridor tapestry with dust on her whiskers and a coin in her teeth: thick, dark, worn almost smooth, with a face on it you don't know. Behind the tapestry there's a gap in the wall just wide enough for a fox.
text [fb4f04] = 余烬从走廊挂毯后面钻出来，胡须上沾着灰，嘴里叼着一枚硬币：厚厚的，黑乎乎的，几乎磨平了，上面的人像你不认识。挂毯后面的墙上有道缝，刚好够一只狐狸钻过去。
# en: A small fox squeezing out of a gap behind a tapestry in a castle corridor, dust on her whiskers and a dark old coin in her teeth.
scene [5013b6] = 城堡走廊里，一只小狐狸从挂毯后的墙缝里钻出来，胡须上沾着灰，嘴里叼着一枚黑乎乎的旧硬币。
# en: Sell it in the village
opt.left.label [14487e] = 拿到村里卖掉
# en: Grimsby turns it over and says it's older than his oldest book, and sends you to the pawnbroker, who pays well and asks where you found it. You say a fox. He writes that down.
opt.left.say.1 [3f1a51] = 格林斯比翻来覆去看了看，说它比他店里最老的书还老，让你去找当铺老板。当铺老板出价很高，还问你是在哪儿找到的。你说是一只狐狸。他把这句话记了下来。
# en: Keep it on the sill for luck
opt.right.label [531f51] = 放在窗台上图个吉利
# en: It sits on your windowsill, and Ember sleeps beside it as if guarding it. Some nights you could swear the face on it has turned to look at the lake.
opt.right.say.1 [fd42fb] = 它就放在你的窗台上，余烬睡在旁边，像在守着它。有些夜里，你敢发誓上面那张脸转过去望着湖了。

@event ember_cold_snap
# en: The Warmest Room in the Tower
title [8d5ad3] = 塔里最暖的房间
# en: The cold has got into the dormitory. Frost on the inside of the glass, everyone's breath showing. Everyone's but yours: Ember is asleep across your feet with her tail glowing, and your room is warm. A student from down the corridor is in your doorway, coughing, in two blankets. "Could I borrow her," they ask, "just for tonight?"
text [98c1ba] = 寒气钻进了宿舍。玻璃里侧结了霜，每个人呼气都冒白烟。只有你不冒：余烬横躺在你脚上睡着，尾巴发着光，你的房间暖烘烘的。走廊那头的一个学生裹着两条毯子站在你门口，咳个不停。“能借她一晚吗？”TA问，“就今晚。”
# en: A frosted dormitory at night, a fox with a glowing tail asleep at the foot of a bed, a shivering student hovering in the doorway with a blanket round their shoulders.
scene [53f451] = 夜里结了霜的宿舍，一只尾巴发光的狐狸睡在床尾，一个瑟瑟发抖的学生披着毯子站在门口。
# en: Lend Ember for the night
opt.left.label [bfb4f1] = 把余烬借出去一晚
# en: Ember goes, with a long look back. You spend a night shivering, and in the morning your neighbour's cough is better, and they tell the whole corridor. Ember comes back at dawn and sleeps on your face to make a point.
opt.left.say.1 [894a5f] = 余烬去了，走时久久地回头看了一眼。你冻了一夜，第二天早上邻居的咳嗽好多了，TA跟整条走廊都说了。余烬天亮时回来，趴在你脸上睡觉，以示抗议。
# en: Keep her by you
opt.right.label [4104df] = 把她留在身边
# en: "Sorry," you say. They nod, and go. You sleep warm. Through the wall you hear them coughing until dawn, and Ember, who heard it too, sleeps with one eye open.
opt.right.say.1 [e6e066] = “对不起，”你说。TA点点头，走了。你睡得很暖。隔着墙，你听见TA一直咳到天亮，余烬也听见了，睁着一只眼睡。
